From: vikas soni <vikassoni@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:47:37 -0700
Subject: Restore texture bindings on every GLES2 draw exit path

PrepareTexturesForRender() binds a black texture in place of each
texture that can't be sampled, and RestoreStateForTextures() rebinds the
tracked textures after the draw. DoMultiDrawArrays() and
DoMultiDrawElements() assumed that bindings only change when
PrepareTexturesForRender() succeeds, but it can fail on a later sampler
(feedback loop or sampler type mismatch) after substituting black
textures for earlier ones. The early returns for that failure, and for a
ValidateAndAdjustDrawBuffers() failure, skipped
RestoreStateForTextures(). The driver's active texture unit and bindings
then no longer matched the decoder's tracked state, so later texture
commands were validated against one texture but executed on another.

Restore the bindings from an absl::Cleanup so that every exit path is
covered. Also unbind the client-side element array buffer in
DoMultiDrawElements() only after ValidateAndAdjustDrawBuffers(), so that
early return can't leave it unbound either.

Separately, RestoreStateForTextures() rebound the unit's most recently
bound target rather than the sampler's target. When they differed, e.g.
a sampler2D reading an incomplete 2D texture on a unit where a cube map
was bound later, the black texture stayed bound even after a successful
draw. Rebind the sampler's target instead.

Bug: 536617330
